Subject: [PATCH] Move reusable line geometry and drawing into Renderer

Adapt the architecture refactor proposed on projectM-visualizer/projectm#1047,
commit ba122baa24cd1794c2a413ec8e308c8ab6e9e4fe (John Neerdael):
https://github.com/projectM-visualizer/projectm/pull/1047

Keep MilkDrop sizing/sample/fade/canvas/dot/thick-pass policy in MilkdropPreset.
Move colored points, padded line batching, drawing and generic shader resources
into Renderer. Extend Mesh with an optional streamed interleaved instance buffer,
custom attributes/divisors/byte offsets and independent instanced draw counts;
use it for both strip lines and motion-vector quads.

Retain the Android engine's constructor-time/prewarmed shader compilation,
cached uniform locations, authored geometry, per-instance styles, prepared
Native-trails replay, packed/floating motion-UV paths and shader-failure fallback.
The motion-vector vertex shader remains preset-owned because it samples its warp
field; the generic fragment shader belongs to Renderer. No public API, preset,
shader arithmetic, version or rendering-policy change is intended.

Add Mesh ownership/upload/layout/draw controls and retain all existing batching
and MilkDrop-policy controls.
